Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(web): playground stage rows, card footers and stream
 re-watch

- The notes block is not rendered when there is nothing to say, so the
  drop surface took a zero-height first row and spilled over the link
  field beneath it; the stage now has three rows without notes, and the
  photo row's minimum matches the drop surface's own.
- The workbench fold has a 480px floor: a short window scrolls the page
  instead of squeezing both columns into a slot nothing fits in.
- Errors and allowance notes sit above the drop surface, not under the fold.
- Card footers wrap at narrow card widths; the gallery aligns cards to
  the top so a text card does not stretch to a picture card's height.
- finish() re-watches a run whose stream dropped before a terminal state
  instead of marking it done; the Add button does not wait on live runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015kWtUp6FyjurHyxcnPnvfS
