From 322520dc7e5fece979499e8455c68f961c269b0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:39:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(web): every screen lays out cleanly from 360px to
 1440px
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Crawled all 53 routes at 360, 390, 768, 1024, 1280 and 1440 with realistic
data and fixed everything that overflowed or squeezed:

- Staff console: the phone rule for the rail was written above the rail's
  own `display: flex`, so it never applied and the sidebar rendered as a
  full-height block above the page. Under 900px the rail is now a sticky
  top bar — brand, avatar and sign-out on one line, the sections as a row
  of chips that scrolls sideways. Stat tiles go single-column under 560px,
  key/value lists stack, the support thread's 300px aside collapses, and
  the two- and three-field dialog rows stack (`.cols2`/`.cols3` replace
  the inline grids).
- Tables: a visually-hidden checkbox input and `.sr-only` labels inside a
  wide table were positioned against an ancestor outside the scroller and
  widened the whole page (providers, templates). The table wrapper and the
  choice row are positioned now, so they stay inside the scroll box.
- Stat values size against their own card (container units), so
  "NGN 84,000" stays on one line at tablet widths instead of pushing the
  card past its column.
- Welcome cards: the centring grid's track sized to the card's longest
  line and pushed it off a phone; the track is now the viewport width and
  the action buttons wrap.
- Developer rows: long endpoint URLs can break, and the row's action
  buttons wrap. Publishing: account actions drop under the handle on a
  phone instead of overlapping it.

No logic changes; the web suite, eslint and the build pass.

